  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper studies quantum differential machine learning on simulators for three finance tasks: a 2-qubit European call learner with 20 training and 10 test points, a 4-qubit Bermudan swaption learner with 201 training and 50 test points, and a 6-qubit basket option learner with 8192 training and 4096 test samples. Reported accuracy is strong in the toy settings, including mean relative errors of 0.069% for European option price and 0.258% for delta, but the paper provides no classical baseline or practical quantum advantage demonstration.",
